ripple_delete_ranges
Cuts SEVERAL time ranges out of the whole timeline as ONE edit — what Clip ▸ Remove Silences… sends. Each pair is put in order (a reversed pair is the same range), the pairs are then MERGED — overlapping and touching alike — and the survivors are cut right to left exactly as ripple_delete_range cuts one. So this is NOT the same as calling that once per pair: two ranges that meet make one shift, not two. It is one undo step however many ranges there are, which is the point. Markers do not move, as under every ripple. An empty list, and a list that merges to nothing, change nothing. detect_silence returns ranges in this shape.
